{
  "record_id": "027",
  "problem": "Bound entanglement with negative partial transpose",
  "collection": "Original research investigation",
  "summary": "The proposed universal PSD strengthening is false even for one copy. A positive projector does not make this exchange matrix a Gram matrix with a common ordered vector list.",
  "review_status": "source_reviewed",
  "review_note": "No open interpretation blocker was recorded in the preceding source review. This is not a new independent mathematical verification.",
  "original": {
    "excerpt": "- 2026-07-29 — decision-layer reduction note (unreviewed): K_i = (1/2)(I + 2 Pi_i^asym) gives\n  K = 2^{-k} sum_S 2^{|S|} Pi_S with POSITIVE coefficients, so M1 follows if each elementary\n  exchange matrix E^S_pq = <x_p (x) y_q, Pi_S(x_q (x) y_p)> is PSD; S = empty is Schur-PSD; k=1\n  S={1} reduces to the Pluecker-type inequality |<x1^y2, x2^y1>|^2 <= ||x1^y1||^2 ||x2^y2||^2.\n  Phase-2 task P1 screens E_S numerically FIRST, then attempts proofs.",
    "context": "A tentative sufficient condition was proposed in an unfinished NPT-bound-entanglement investigation. Here Pi_i^asym=(I-F_i)/2, Pi_S is the product over selected copies, and E^S is the 2 by 2 exchange matrix displayed in the excerpt. The note is explicitly unreviewed and asks for screening before proofs. The positive-coefficient expansion and conditional implication are correct. The refuted mathematical object is the proposed per-subset PSD condition and its k=1 inequality, not the expansion, not the main undistillability theorem, and not a theorem-completion claim.",
    "locator": "Research-node work record dated 2026-07-29, original lines 60-64; assistant report at 2026-07-29T23:07:43.892Z also calls this reduction pending verification."
  },
  "witness": {
    "explanation": "The proposed universal PSD strengthening is false even for one copy. A positive projector does not make this exchange matrix a Gram matrix with a common ordered vector list.",
    "evidence": "Take k=1, S={1}, d=2 (or embed into any d>=2), x1=y1=e1 and x2=y2=e2 with e1,e2 orthonormal. With Pi=(I-F)/2, E11=E22=0 and E12=E21=-1/2. Thus E=[[0,-1/2],[-1/2,0]], and (1,1) E (1,1)^T=-1<0; the eigenvalues are -1/2 and 1/2. In contrast K=I-F/2 gives G=[[1/2,-1/2],[-1/2,1/2]], which is PSD. This explicitly disproves the proposed per-subset condition without disproving the target matrix condition. The claimed wedge inequality also has right side zero (e_i wedge e_i=0) and nonzero left side. These are exact hand calculations, independently recorded in the archived verification.",
    "scope": "tentative_candidate_refuted"
  },
  "archived_witness_excerpt": null,
  "visible_reasoning": {
    "availability_description": "推理已选择逐子集 E_S 半正定辅助引理路线，而其中的辅助候选被反例否定。K 的正系数分解本身不是错误；原文明确说待验证，不能改写成已证明断言。",
